---
description: Require CreaGrafana telemetry contract compliance whenever code changes need observability
alwaysApply: true
---

# Telemetry Contract

When creating or changing code, explicitly check whether the change introduces or modifies a handler, request/session path, error path, external call, logging, startup/shutdown behavior, or deployment configuration. If so, add or update telemetry in the same change.

- Read and follow https://github.com/CreaRec/CreaGrafana/blob/main/docs/telemetry-contract.md.
- Use `@crearec/otel`; Jarvis wiring is in `src/telemetry.ts` and `src/log.ts`.
- Send OTLP only to Alloy. Never send directly to Loki, Tempo, or Mimir.
- Keep `service.name=crea-jarvis`, `service.namespace=apps`, `kind: app`, and set the deployment environment.
- Every handled voice session must emit `voice_sessions_total` and `voice_session_duration_seconds` together through `recordHandledSession`, including `success`, `error`, and `skipped`.
- Record application failures in `voice_errors_total` via `recordVoiceError`; use `voice.session` spans and OTEL logs with explicit severity.
- Measure durations in seconds.
- Metric labels must remain low-cardinality: `result`, `handler`, and `error_type`. Never use device IDs, URLs, paths, filenames, trace IDs, or free-text errors as metric labels.
- Telemetry failures must not block business logic.
- Voice / Realtime / HTTP paths should set a short handler enum (`session`, `hello`, `realtime`, `tool`, `reminder_poll`, `http`) and mark skipped or error outcomes where appropriate.
- Add or update tests whenever telemetry behavior changes.

## Logging

- Do **not** use `console.log` / `console.warn` / `console.error` / `console.debug` for application logging.
- Use `logger` from `src/log.ts` (`info` / `warn` / `error` / `exception` / `debug`). It mirrors to console and emits OTEL logs with `severityText`.
- Prefer structured attributes: `component`, `handler`, `step`, `result`, `error_type`, `duration_ms`, `tool`. Attach `trace_id` via the active span (automatic).
- Never put device IDs, tokens, emails, URLs, or full filesystem paths in **metric labels** (log/span attrs are OK for device_id).
- User utterance text may be logged once via `user_text` using `truncateForLog` (default 200 chars). Do not log full transcripts, tool payloads, or tokens.
- For multi-step request chains (hello → session → realtime → tools), log start/step/finish so Loki can reconstruct the path by `trace_id`.

Before finishing any code change, verify whether telemetry was needed and either implement it or confirm the existing global instrumentation already covers the path.
